Resume interrupted process streams for agent-substrate/env.

Ported from Samuel Huber's environment reliability patches. Applies to env
56424de763f91daa6b6c38f6249bacef1d82e5e1 after patches 0001 through 0004.

Reopen output at delivered byte offsets after router route/idle timeouts or
transient stream cuts. Reopen stdin on the next write, and propagate an
upstream input-stream cut immediately from the API. Reconnect probes and
repeated failures without progress are bounded. Regression tests exercise
both route-timeout and idle-timeout responses. Guest tests use isolated
spool directories instead of deleting another package's shared test spool.

Rebased over ate-nix's PTY terminal-restoration fix: retain exitCodeError and
its tests. Follow consumes output through the exit message before returning,
so the earlier separate Wait/output-drain loop and timer are no longer needed.

